INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(4500, 0, 45, 0, 0, 0, 'Arathi Highlands', 'The Arathi Highlands are a country of rolling green hills and scattered pines, and the birthplace of the first human nation. Here Thoradin united the human tribes into the Empire of Arathor and raised Strom, its first capital, with a great wall to hold back the Amani trolls. The Trollbane kings who later ruled Stromgarde from the old capital warred with the Witherbark trolls for generations. Those days are gone. King Thoras Trollbane is dead and his city lies in ruins, carved up between Prince Galen''s militia, the outlaws of the Syndicate and the Boulderfist ogres. The last soldiers of Stromgarde hold Refuge Pointe in the heart of the highlands, while in the northeast the Horde has rebuilt Hammerfall on the site of an old orc internment camp. Witherbark warbands and ogres press them all. Beneath the hills, a voice calls out through glowing crystals, begging to be set free, and on the southern coast a pirate crew sits marooned in Faldir''s Cove.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Arathi_Highlands (Thoradin, Arathor, Strom, Thoradin''s Wall, Trollbane feud with Witherbark, Stromgarde overrun, Refuge Pointe, Hammerfall internment camp); quest 638 description (Thoras dead, Stromgarde in ruins); quest 681 description (city divided three ways); quest 642 description; quest 663 description'),
(4501, 1, 45, 1, 0, 0, 'Thoradin''s Wall', 'From the highlands, Thoradin''s Wall marks the western edge of the land, a long line of weathered stone between Arathi and the foothills beyond. King Thoradin raised it to guard Strom, the first human capital, and the ruins of that city, now called Stromgarde, still lie near it. The wall has held no army back for a very long time. Highland striders hunt along its foot and plains creepers crawl among its fallen stones. Where Thoradin once feared troll warbands, the highlands now face ogres, outlaws and the Witherbark all at once, and the old barrier stops none of them.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Thoradin''s_Wall (built by Thoradin near Strom against Amani incursions; separates Arathi from Hillsbrad; heavily damaged and in ruins in original WoW); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Arathi_Highlands (collapsed wall); posarea.py: area 1857 found on the western edge between Hillsbrad and Arathi; zone_areas: Highland Strider 2559 and Plains Creeper 2563 spawn in area 1857'),
(4502, 1, 45, 2, 0, 0, 'Northfold Manor', 'Northfold Manor is a farm estate on the northwestern edge of the highlands. After Stromgarde fell, the Syndicate seized it as an outpost, and highwaymen, mercenaries and pathstalkers now hold its fields and barns. From here the outlaws command the country between Refuge Pointe and Southshore, so that the supplies the Stromgarde defenders need from Hillsbrad rarely get through. Worse things have happened here than banditry. The shaman Tor''gan of Hammerfall traced a burning unease in his blood to the manor and found the traces of demonic summoning, with a spent bloodstone amulet lying on the ground. A rarely seen outlaw called Singer lurks in the small house.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Northfold_Manor (farm, Syndicate outpost after Stromgarde fell, Singer in the small house); quest 681 description (Syndicate holds territory between Refuge Pointe and Southshore); quest 671 description and reward text; DB spawns: Syndicate Highwayman 2586, Mercenary 2589, Pathstalker 2587 in area 313; Singer 2600 (rare) at 32.3,31.0'),
(4503, 1, 45, 3, 0, 0, 'Boulder''gor', 'Boulder''gor is an ogre mound in the western highlands, northeast of the ruins of Stromgarde. Boulderfist ogres and enforcers crowd its camps, and Witherbark trolls come and go among them, a sign of the pact the two peoples have made against their common enemies. A brutish ogre named Kovork is sometimes found there. For the Horde, the mound serves as a proving ground: Tallow of Tarren Mill sends would-be recruits here to test their strength before they are trusted to join the defenders of Hammerfall.', 'quest 676 description and reward text (ogre mound northeast of Stromgarde, Tallow''s test); DB spawns in area 1858: Boulderfist Ogre 2562 x17, Boulderfist Enforcer 2564 x16, Witherbark Troll 2552, Witch Doctor 2555, Shadowcaster 2553, Kovork 2603 (rare) at 33.7,44.1; quest 677 description (Witherbark and Boulderfist working together); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Boulderfist_clan (Tallow and Boulder''gor)'),
(4504, 1, 45, 4, 0, 0, 'The Circles of Binding', 'Four rings of standing stones lie scattered across the highlands: the Circles of West, East and Outer Binding, and the strongest of them, the Circle of Inner Binding, close to the ruins of Stromgarde. Each holds a Stone of Binding, and together they pin something deep beneath the earth. Elemental exiles keep watch over them: creatures of flame at the western circle, of water in the east, of thunder at the outer ring and of rumbling stone at the inner one, where a Keystone stands among the stones as a final lock. Near the eastern circle walks Fozruk, a stone watcher who carries the key to that lock, attended by a small band of kobolds.', 'quest 651 description and objectives (four Stones of Binding, Inner the strongest, keys from West, East, Outer); quest 652 description (Keystone, Fozruk the stone watcher, Rod of Order); DB spawns: Burning Exile 2760 in 334, Cresting Exile 2761 in 333, Thundering Exile 2762 in 336, Rumbling Exile 2592 in 335; Stones 2689/2691/2690/2702 and Keystone 2688; Fozruk 2611 with kobolds Sleeby 2764, Znort 2765, Feeboz 4063 in area 333; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Circle_of_Inner_Binding (southern highlands near Stromgarde, strongest stone); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Fozruk (mountain giant, had three kobolds with him until 4.0.3a)'),
(4505, 1, 45, 5, 0, 0, 'Stromgarde Keep', 'Once Strom, the first capital of humankind, Stromgarde was long the seat of the Trollbane kings. Now it is a ruin and a battlefield. Prince Galen Trollbane''s militia holds the quarter around the chapel and the Sanctum behind it, where King Thoras lies entombed with the sword Trol''kalar. The Syndicate under Lord Falconcrest commands the inner keep, while the Boulderfist ogres, Witherbark berserkers at their side, have taken the old mage district and the Tower of Arathor, whose master, Archmage Trelane, tried to hold it and failed. None of the three can drive out the others, and the bloody stalemate grinds on while the defenders dwindle.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Stromgarde_Keep (Strom as Arathor''s capital, Trollbane house, three-way division, Falconcrest, Trelane); quest 681 description (bloody stalemate, forces dwindle); quest 645 description (remains entombed in the Sanctum behind the chapel); quest 644 description (Galen in a chapel in the militia-held districts); quest 690 description (Trelane failed to hold the Tower); DB spawns in area 324: Galen 2607, Falconcrest 2597, Or''Kalar 2773 near the tower, Witherbark Berserker 2558 x3'),
(4506, 1, 45, 6, 0, 0, 'Faldir''s Cove', 'On the rugged southern coast lies Faldir''s Cove, named, it seems, for Faldir, the descendant of Thoradin who led his followers away from Arathor to found the kingdom of Stormwind. Today it shelters the Harbinger, the one ship of Captain Shakes O''Breen''s Blackwater Raiders to come in safely. The pirates sailed from Booty Bay after a lost elven treasure, but as the other two ships followed the Harbinger in, the sea rumbled, the tide fell away and both were wrecked on the reef. The survivors now camp beside the water with a pair of gnomish inventors, unable to leave until the tide rises and the naga stop watching.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Faldir''s_Cove (named after Faldir; Blackwater Raiders expedition; Harbinger); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Arathi_Highlands (Thoradin''s descendants led by Faldir founded Stormwind); quest 663 description and reward text; quest 669 description (tide too low, creatures watching); DB spawns in area 327: Shakes O''Breen 2610, Draxlegauge 2774, Phizzlethorpe 2768, Steelgut 2769, Nilzlix 2767, Lolo 2766'),
(4507, 1, 45, 7, 0, 0, 'The Drowned Reef', 'Off the coast southwest of Faldir''s Cove lies the Drowned Reef, and it is not only a reef. Sunken stonework, something like a temple, lies beneath the waves, guarded by the Daggerspine naga, and it is said the strange tide that wrecked the Blackwater Raiders was their doing. The Maiden''s Folly and the Spirit of Silverpine ran aground on it and sank so fast that few escaped, and the naga slew the survivors in the water. The ships'' logs and charts still lie in the wrecks, and gems from an old elven treasure, calcified into stone, are scattered across the sea floor. A naga called Prince Nazjak hunts these waters.', 'quest 662 description (ships ran aground on some sort of temple in the reef, sank quickly; logs and charts); quest 664 description (naga killed all the survivors); quest 666 description (gems calcified into stone); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Faldir''s_Cove (tide caused by the naga guarding sunken ruins); DB spawns in area 328: Daggerspine Raider 2595 x42, Sorceress 2596 x10, Prince Nazjak 2779 (rare) at 19.4,90.2'),
(4508, 1, 45, 8, 0, 0, 'Refuge Pointe', 'Refuge Pointe, in the heart of the highlands, is the last stronghold of the kingdom of Stromgarde. When the city fell, the remnants of its army refused to abandon the land and withdrew here, and under Captain Nials they have sworn not to leave until the king''s banner flies over Stromgarde once more. It is a spare camp of tents, a forge, a few merchants and a gryphon roost, ringed by defenders, and its wanted board posts the militia''s bounties on Syndicate leaders. Two agents of Archmage Malin of Stormwind, the dwarf Skuerto and Apprentice Kryten, have also made camp here, sent to recover what Archmage Trelane left behind when the city fell.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Refuge_Pointe (Stromic army remnants stayed to retake their capital; central highlands; inn in a tent, forge); quest 634 reward text (Stromgarde has fallen, will not leave until the banner of the King is raised); quest 691 description; DB spawns in area 320: Refuge Pointe Defender 10696 x22, Cedrik Prose 2835 gryphon master, Wanted Board 2713, merchants; quest 690 description (Trelane''s items), quest 691 completion text (dwarven companion)'),
(4509, 1, 45, 9, 0, 0, 'Dabyrie''s Farmstead', 'In the north of the highlands stands Dabyrie''s Farmstead, home of a family that still holds to the kingdom of Stromgarde. Kenata Dabyrie keeps the farm with her children Fardel and Marcel, and a crew of laborers works the fields under the protection of the Dabyrie Militia. Not everyone is glad that they prospered. In the Undercity, the Forsaken Genavie Callow, who lost her family to the plague and saw her estate looted and burned in the war, swears the Dabyries stole the last precious things she owned, and she wants all of their heads for it.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dabyrie''s_Farmstead (Kenata and her children Fardel and Marcel, Stromgarde, Dabyrie Militia, Genavie Callow''s grudge); quest 1164 description, completion and reward text (Genavie Callow, started in the Undercity, Horde only); DB spawns in area 315: Dabyrie Laborer 2582 x26, Dabyrie Militia 2581 x9, Fardel 4479, Kenata 4480, Marcel 4481 (faction 123); Genavie Callow 4486 at 1561,260 (Undercity); waypoint_data 145720: Valorcall''s path runs only between Stromgarde (324) and Refuge Pointe (320)'),
(4510, 1, 45, 10, 0, 0, 'Go''Shek Farm', 'Go''Shek Farm, in the east of the highlands, has been taken over by the Horde to help feed Hammerfall, and peons work its fields under the watch of grunts. Not all of its business is farming. Forsaken bodyguards stand over a small house to the south, where Apothecary Jorell works in secret and promises anyone who troubles him that he will find a use for their body once they are dead. Couriers slip away from the house toward Tarren Mill, and the farm has drawn quiet watchers from Southshore who suspect the Forsaken are brewing something terrible.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Go''Shek_Farm (Forsaken and Hammerfall orcs took it; supplies Hammerfall; Jorell''s experiments, a new plague); quests 657, 658, 659, 661 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_text 2733 (Jorell); DB spawns in area 314: Hammerfall Peon 2618 x27, Grunt 2619 x16, Forsaken Bodyguard 2721 x4, Apothecary Jorell 2733 at 60.1,59.3, Forsaken Courier 2714, Quae 2712, Kinelory 2713'),
(4511, 1, 45, 11, 0, 0, 'Hammerfall', 'Hammerfall stands in the northeast of the highlands on ground the orcs remember with bitterness. After the Second War this was one of the largest of the human internment camps, where captured orcs were held behind wood and steel. Thrall and Orgrim Doomhammer stormed it to free the prisoners, and in that battle a knight charged Doomhammer from behind and ran him through with his lance, a mortal wound. When the Horde returned to the highlands, it raised an outpost on the ruins and named it in the fallen warchief''s honor. Now Drum Fel leads its defense against the Boulderfist ogres and Witherbark trolls, who have joined forces to drive the Horde out.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Hammerfall (one of the largest internment camps, freed by Thrall and Doomhammer, Doomhammer mortally wounded by a knight''s lance, named in his honor, Drum Fel); quest 655 description and reward text; quest 638 description (northeastern Arathi); quest 677 description'),
(4512, 1, 45, 12, 0, 0, 'Drywhisker Gorge', 'Drywhisker Gorge cuts into the hills east of Hammerfall and ends in a cave held by the Drywhisker kobolds. They are allies of the giants who keep a prisoner beneath Arathi, and they carry motes of that prisoner''s power. Nearby, a cluster of iridescent shards juts from the rock, much like the Shards of Myzrael, though it lacks their reassuring warmth. The gorge is also the only known source of lesser bloodstone ore, and the kobold geomancer Flintdagger is sometimes seen among the diggers and surveyors.', 'quest 642 description (Drywhisker kobolds allies of the giants, shard in their gorge, Motes of Myzrael); quest 642 completion text (looks like the Shards of Myzrael without the same feeling); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Drywhisker_Gorge (east of Hammerfall, cave, only source of Lesser Bloodstone Ore before Cataclysm); DB spawns in area 318: Drywhisker Kobold 2572, Digger 2574, Surveyor 2573, Geomancer Flintdagger 2609 (rare); Lesser Bloodstone Deposit 2653 and Iridescent Shards 2701 at 83-87,29-34'),
(4513, 1, 45, 13, 0, 0, 'Witherbark Village', 'In the southeast of the highlands, around a small lake, lies Witherbark Village, home of the forest trolls who have been sworn enemies of Stromgarde for generations. Axe throwers, headhunters and witch doctors fill the huts, while the shadow hunters, the strongest of whom carry a special knife earned in their rites of passage, keep to a large cavern behind the village where the tribe''s leaders are often found, among them the warband leader Zalas Witherbark. A second warband leader, Nimar the Slayer, also stalks the village. The Witherbark have made common cause with the Boulderfist ogres, and together they have set out to drive the Horde from Hammerfall.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Witherbark_Village (southeast, small lake, cavern with Zalas and shadow hunters); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Witherbark_tribe (sworn enemies of Stromgarde, Boulderfist alliance); quest 691 completion text (shadow hunters'' knife after rites of passage); quest 677 description; DB spawns in area 317: Headhunter 2556, Axe Thrower 2554, Witch Doctor 2555, Shadow Hunter 2557, Zalas Witherbark 2605 and Nimar the Slayer 2606 (rares, several spawn points)'),
(4514, 1, 45, 14, 0, 0, 'Boulderfist Hall', 'Boulderfist Hall is an ogre stronghold in the south of the highlands, east of the Thandol Span. Brutes and magi of the Boulderfist clan hold it, and the defenders of Hammerfall count them a harder foe than the Witherbark. A hulking ogre known as Molok the Crusher is sometimes found there. Of late, one of the hall''s ogres, Kor''gresh Coldrage, has been hurling blasts of ice at his own kin to keep them in line, using a wand that once belonged to Archmage Trelane of Stromgarde.', 'quest 693 description (south of Refuge Pointe, east of Thandol Span; Kor''gresh''s ice blasts); quest 678 description (maulers and magi a greater challenge); DB spawns in area 316: Boulderfist Brute 2566 x18, Magus 2567 x8, Kor''gresh Coldrage 2793, Molok the Crusher 2604 (rare)'),
(4515, 1, 45, 15, 0, 0, 'Thandol Span', 'The Thandol Span comes to ground at the southern tip of the highlands, and the Arathi end of the crossing is no safer than the Wetlands side. Dark Iron shadowcasters, bombardiers and suppliers have made camp on the slopes just beyond the bridge. Out on the span, the dwarf sentry Foggy MacKreel nurses a sore head. He drank too much moonshine and slept through his watch, and recalls only a rumbling overhead, as if a whole brigade of siege engines had rolled past. He fears Longbraid would have his head if he knew, and frets about a moonshine debt he owes a brewmeister in Southshore.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Thandol_Span (built by Ironforge dwarves linking Khaz Modan and Lordaeron; Dark Iron attack; Foggy MacKreel on the ruined bridge); quest 633 description (cache of explosives just across the Thandol Span in Arathi); quest 647 description (Foggy passed out during his watch, rumbling); DB spawns: Foggy MacKreel 2696 in area 880; Dark Iron Shadowcaster 2577, Bombardier 4062, Supplier 2575 and Cache of Explosives 2704 at 48-50,87-89; quest 647 description and reward text (Longbraid, debt to Brewmeister Bilger in Southshore)'),
(4516, 2, 45, 1, 1, 0, 'Captain Nials', 'Captain Nials commands the remnants of the Stromgarde army at Refuge Pointe. Her city has fallen, and honor and duty bind her soldiers to the highlands until the king''s banner flies over Stromgarde once more, so firmly that she turned away the dwarves of the Wetlands when they asked for aid. She knows the war is going badly, her ranks thinning while the enemy grows. When the badges of her fallen soldiers are taken back from the Syndicate, she reads their names aloud one by one and sighs that so many have been lost, and so many more must be before the battle ends. Then she sends word to their families.', 'quest 634 reward text; quest 681 description; quest 682 reward text; creature_text 2700 (reading the names, So many lost); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Refuge_Pointe (Captain Nials, she)'),
(4517, 2, 45, 2, 2, 0, 'Prince Galen Trollbane', 'Galen Trollbane is the son of King Thoras Trollbane and heir to a kingdom in ruins. With his father dead, he leads the militia that holds part of Stromgarde, keeping to a chapel deep in the city beside the Sanctum where Thoras lies entombed with the ancestral sword Trol''kalar. To guard the tomb, the sigils that unseal it were divided among the survivors: the sigil of Thoradin Galen broke into five pieces and gave to his defenders, the sigil of Arathor went to his cavalry leader Valorcall, and the sigil of Trollbane he keeps on his own person. He is well guarded and a capable warrior in his own right.', 'quest 640 description (Galen divided the sigil of Thoradin); quest 639 description (sigils divided among the survivors); quest 643 description (Valorcall); quest 644 description (Galen holds the final sigil in a chapel, well protected); quest 645 description (Sanctum behind the chapel); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Galen_Trollbane (son and heir of Thoras, led the defenders, guarded the crypt)'),
(4518, 2, 45, 3, 0, 0, 'Lord Falconcrest and Otto', 'The Syndicate is a brotherhood of outlaws led by nobles of fallen Alterac, and in the Arathi Highlands its efforts are directed by Lord Falconcrest from the ruins of Stromgarde. His outlaws hold the inner keep, and the Syndicate''s leaders pay their rabble gold for every badge taken from a dead Stromgarde soldier. At Falconcrest''s side stands his bodyguard Otto, no strategist but a fierce fighter who has killed dozens of the city''s defenders, and who assures his master that everything is going as planned. The Stromgarde militia has put a price on both their heads.', 'quest 685 description; quest 682 description (bounty on Stromgarde badges); creature_text 2597, 2599; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Syndicate (led by nobles of fallen Alterac; Falconcrest commands in Stromgarde); DB spawns: Falconcrest 2597 and Otto 2599 at 26,65.7 in area 324'),
(4519, 2, 45, 4, 0, 0, 'Marez Cowl', 'Marez Cowl is a warlock and a high-ranking advisor and operative of the Syndicate, last seen in the outlaw-held quarter of Stromgarde. She traffics openly with demons. With a bloodstone orb she has called them forth in great numbers, a power the shaman Tor''gan of Hammerfall feels as a burning in his own blood. Captain Nials has heard it whispered that Marez is an emissary between the Syndicate and some other, darker power. Refuge Pointe and Hammerfall agree on little, but both want her dead.', 'quest 684 description and reward text (high-level advisor and operative, warlock trafficking with demons, emissary to a darker power); quest 673 description and reward text (warlock in Stromgarde summoning demons with a bloodstone orb); quest 671 completion text (burning in the blood); DB spawns: Marez Cowl 2783 at 29.6,63 in area 324'),
(4520, 2, 45, 5, 2, 0, 'Drum Fel and Korin Fel', 'Drum Fel leads the defense of Hammerfall, a hard warrior with little patience for the untested and no time even to sharpen his axe. He sends every able fighter against the Witherbark and Boulderfist warbands that besiege the outpost, praising courage and scorning cowardice in equal measure, and believes Hammerfall will thrive in the highlands once its enemies are broken. His wife, Korin Fel, is a seer who loves him enough to deceive him. Her auguries revealed that the ogre Or''Kalar has laid a trap for her husband, and she has hidden every sign of the ogre from Drum, knowing he would rush off to face his old foe.', 'quests 676, 677, 678, 679 (descriptions, completion and reward texts); quest 680 description and completion text; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Hammerfall (Drum Fel led the settlement, believed it would thrive)'),
(4521, 2, 45, 6, 2, 0, 'Gor''mul', 'Gor''mul is an orc warrior of the old Horde who was once a prisoner in the internment camp that stood where Hammerfall is now. He saw Orgrim Doomhammer come in his midnight plate to free the camp, and saw a knight on horseback run the Warchief through from behind. As the earth shook and the other prisoners escaped, Gor''mul was left behind, and he wandered alone and without hope for years until the Horde returned. Bitter that he was not allowed to die beside his Warchief, he scorned every charm brought to cheer him, until the shaman Tor''gan let him feel the guile of the raptor and the strength the shamans had found again.', 'quest 655 description and reward text; quests 674, 675, 702, 847 (descriptions and texts); creature_text 2792; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Gor''mul (orc warrior of the Old Horde)'),
(4522, 2, 45, 7, 2, 0, 'Tor''gan', 'Tor''gan is a troll shaman of Hammerfall, a practitioner of the shamanic magic the Horde has found anew under its young Warchief Thrall. He has spent much patience on Gor''mul, crafting amulets and orbs filled with the spirit of the raptor in the hope of waking the warrior within. He feels fouler magic too. A burning in his blood led him to Northfold Manor and the traces of demonic summoning there, and to the warlock in Stromgarde whose bloodstone orb he vowed to destroy. When the five shattered pieces of the sigil of Thoradin were laid before him, he bound them whole again, and found it easier than he expected.', 'quest 640 description (Tor''gan, the troll shaman) and reward text; quests 671, 672, 673, 701 (descriptions and reward texts); quest 847 reward text; creature_text 2706 (easier than I expected)'),
(4523, 2, 45, 8, 0, 0, 'Or''Kalar', 'Or''Kalar is a Boulderfist ogre who leads his clan''s forces in Stromgarde, a pawn of Mug''thol, and he lurks near the Tower of Arathor. Years ago he was beaten by Drum Fel of Hammerfall, and he has hated him ever since. The attacks on Hammerfall are part of his design, a trap meant to draw Drum Fel out to his death. Only Drum''s wife Korin knows it. She saw the plot in her auguries and hid all signs of the ogre from her husband, quietly seeking someone else to end the threat.', 'quest 680 description, completion and reward texts (Mug''thol''s pawn, hatred of Drum Fel, trap, near the Tower of Arathor, his death stops the attacks); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Boulderfist_clan (Or''Kalar led the Boulderfist forces in Stromgarde, answers to Mug''thol); DB spawns: Or''Kalar 2773, 7 spawn points at 18-21,65-69 in area 324'),
(4524, 2, 45, 9, 0, 0, 'Myzrael', 'Myzrael calls herself a princess of the earth, held captive deep beneath the Arathi Highlands by the giants. Her only voice in the world above comes through crystal shards that break the surface in the northern hills, and through them she pleads for rescue, stirring a feeling of warmth and safety in all who listen. Those who set her free learn too late what she is. Summoned before her strength has returned, she turns on her rescuer and names them a fool for helping her. She has other servants already: cultists of the Twilight''s Hammer revere her as their Lady and know how she may be called to the surface.', 'quest 642 description; quest 635 description (vision of the northern mountains); quest 656 description and reward text (warmth and security); creature_text 2755; quests 653, 687, 688 (Twilight''s Hammer, the Lady); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Myzrael (earth elemental princess imprisoned by giants)'),
(4525, 2, 45, 10, 0, 0, 'Shakes O''Breen', 'Captain Shakes O''Breen of the Blackwater Raiders led three ships out of Booty Bay to Faldir''s Cove, steered by one of Professor Phizzlethorpe''s contraptions toward a lost elven treasure. Only his own ship, the Harbinger, came through. He dreads what Fleet Master Seahorn will say about the loss, though Seahorn calls him the right captain for the job. O''Breen does not value his own life above his crew''s, but he knows they cannot reach home without his knowledge of the seas, so when the naga gather for an attack he stands on the high ground beside the cannon to drive them back.', 'quest 663 reward text; quest 667 description; quest 669 description and reward text; creature_text 2610; DB: Cannon 113531 at 32.1,80.7'),
(4526, 3, 45, 1, 1, 0, 'The Defenders of Stromgarde', 'From Refuge Pointe, Captain Nials fights a war she is losing. Her soldiers, the Syndicate and the ogres have divided Stromgarde in a bloody stalemate, and while her ranks thin, the enemy''s swell. Help must come from Southshore, but the Syndicate holds the land between, so the outlaws of Northfold Manor must be cleared before the supply trains can get through. Inside the city, Syndicate leaders pay their rabble gold for every badge cut from a fallen militiaman, and Nials wants each one returned, so that families may at least know their loved ones died in battle. The wanted board at Refuge Pointe names the true targets: Marez Cowl, a warlock rumored to deal with some darker power, and Lord Falconcrest and his bodyguard Otto, whose deaths would throw the Syndicate''s efforts in the highlands into disarray.', 'quests 681, 682, 684, 685 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_text 2700; gameobject_queststarter: Wanted Board 2713 starts 684 and 685'),
(4527, 3, 45, 2, 1, 0, 'Trelane''s Treasures', 'When Stromgarde fell, Archmage Trelane tried and failed to hold the Tower of Arathor, then fled to Stormwind, leaving his belongings behind. His former apprentice, Archmage Malin, sent two agents to recover them: the gruff dwarf Skuerto and Apprentice Kryten, who set up camp at Refuge Pointe. While Kryten sought Witherbark reagents for Malin, Skuerto went scouting and came back from Boulderfist Hall looking as if he had tangled with the ogres, having learned that the ogre Kor''gresh Coldrage had taken Trelane''s Wand of Invocation and was close to mastering it. With the wand recovered, the rest lay in the tower itself, now overrun by ogres. A gem the Boulderfist shaman had stolen from the tower, enchanted by Kryten and pressed to a pedestal at its foot, woke the tower''s old defenses, and Trelane''s phylactery, orb and ember agate were carried out of their chests and home to a delighted Malin.', 'quests 690, 691, 693, 694, 695, 696, 697 (descriptions and reward texts); npc_text 3293, 3294 (Kryten); DB: Runed Pedestal 2715 and Trelane''s Chest 2716, Footlocker 2717, Lockbox 2718 at 18,67-69; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Stromgarde_Keep (Trelane failed to defend the Tower and exiled himself to Stormwind)'),
(4528, 3, 45, 3, 2, 0, 'Hammerfall Besieged', 'Hammerfall is under constant attack. In Tarren Mill, Tallow tests would-be defenders against the ogres of Boulder''gor before sending them to Drum Fel, who names the enemy plainly: the Witherbark trolls, who turned their backs on the Horde, and the Boulderfist ogres, who would make meat and bedding of orcs, have joined forces to drive Hammerfall from the land. Drum''s champions carry the war to the Witherbark camps to the south, then to the brutes and magi of the ogre lair toward the dwarven bridge, and finally to the Boulderfist lords and shaman who direct the raids from the ruins of Stromgarde. Drum''s wife Korin knows what he does not: the attacks are the work of Or''Kalar, an ogre who has hated her husband since Drum defeated him years ago and has laid a trap for him. Quietly, she asks for Or''Kalar''s head instead.', 'quests 676, 677, 678, 679, 680 (descriptions, completion and reward texts)'),
(4529, 3, 45, 4, 2, 0, 'Trol''kalar', 'In the days of Arathor, Lord Ignaeus of Strom, called Trollbane, rode against the trolls with Trol''kalar, whose name means troll slayer, and for generations Strom and Arathor ravaged the trolls with it. With Thoras Trollbane dead and Stromgarde in ruins, Vol''jin resolved to take the sword for the Darkspear and turn it on the trolls of Zul''Gurub, and sent the hunter Zengu to Hammerfall to see it done. The blade lay sealed in Thoras''s tomb behind wards only the sigils could break. The sigil of Strom was taken from the Syndicate, who had stolen it. The sigil of Thoradin, split into five among the city''s defenders, was gathered and bound whole by Tor''gan. The sigil of Arathor was won from Lieutenant Valorcall, and the last from Prince Galen himself, slain in his chapel. Joined, they became the Sigil of Ignaeus, and at its touch the stone hands of the tomb released the sword, bound for Nimboya at Grom''gol.', 'quests 638, 639, 640, 641, 643, 644, 645, 646 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_text 2706; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Trol''kalar (pre-Cataclysm sections)'),
(4530, 3, 45, 5, 0, 0, 'The Princess Beneath the Stones', 'Those who touch the Shards of Myzrael in the northern hills hear a voice pleading for help: a princess of the earth, she says, imprisoned far below by the giants. To strengthen her, the Drywhisker kobolds are robbed of the motes of her power and a second cluster of shards in their gorge is woken. Next come the Stones of Binding. Keys taken from the circles of West, East and Outer Binding open the Stone of Inner Binding, and the Rod of Order, won from the stone watcher Fozruk, unlocks the Keystone. Myzrael cries out that she is free, and sends her rescuer to her servants in the Twilight''s Hammer, who know how she may be called to the surface. That road leads to the Badlands and Theldurin the Lost, and in the end the summons is turned against her: called up at the Shards before her power is whole, Myzrael is defeated and bound again in her own Eldritch Shackles, and the shards pulse now with open menace.', 'quests 635, 642, 651, 652, 653, 688, 687, 692, 656 (descriptions and reward texts); creature_text 2755; gameobject_queststarter: Shards of Myzrael 138492 starts 642; Iridescent Shards 2701, Stone of Inner Binding 2702, Keystone 2688'),
(4531, 3, 45, 6, 0, 0, 'The Blackwater Expedition', 'Shakes O''Breen''s Blackwater Raiders came to Faldir''s Cove expecting to stay only a few hours, just long enough to raise a lost elven treasure and sail home to Booty Bay. Instead the sea rumbled, the tide fell away and two of their three ships broke apart on the Drowned Reef. Now the crew needs help. First Mate Nilzlix wants the wrecks'' logs and charts recovered before prying eyes find them, and Captain Steelgut, who lost his Maiden''s Folly and woke on the shore after the naga slew his crew, wants the Daggerspine made to pay. The gnomes Phizzlethorpe and Draxlegauge charge a pair of goggles from a cursed rune stone in a cave up the hill, and through them the calcified elven gems on the sea floor shine plainly. When the naga mass for an attack, O''Breen holds the high ground with a cannon, then sends a sample gem to Fleet Master Seahorn as proof of the find.', 'quests 662 to 670 (descriptions, completion and reward texts); creature_text 2768, 2610');
